# Logging

All plugin logging and debugging goes through [`model/logger.ts`](model/logger.ts). Do not use `console.log`, `console.error`, `console.warn`, or ad-hoc log helpers.

## API

```typescript
import {log, error} from "../model/logger"; // adjust relative path

log("area", "message", { kind?, triggerId?, animationId?, trainIndex?, carIndex?, detail? });
error("area", "message", detail?, meta?); // failures; prefer over throwing on load/tick paths
```

- `area`: short source tag (`trigger`, `animation`, `step`, `tick`, `runtimeState`, …)
- `log`: expected lifecycle / info events
- `error`: real failures; pass `meta.triggerId` / `meta.animationId` for Logs-tab filters

OpenRCT2’s console only has `log`; the logger prefixes errors as `[Animator][error][area]`. Entries also go to the in-memory buffer shown on the Logs tab.

## Allowed lifecycle `log` kinds

Use structured `kind` when applicable:

- `triggerFired` — via `reportTriggerFired` / trigger success paths
- `animationStarted` — when a run is actually started
- `stepStarted` — when a step begins on a run
- `animationConcluded` — when a run is removed (include `endReason`)

Do **not** add variable-change spam unless Simon explicitly asks.

Stamp `triggerId` / `animationId` on runtime lifecycle logs and errors so the Logs tab filters work.

## Logs tab

- Filters: **All Triggers** / **All Animations** (AND). Reset both to All when the Animator window opens.
- UI reads the shared buffer via `subscribe` / `getRecentLogs` / `clearLogs`. Do not keep a parallel observe/fire-only buffer.

## Do / don’t

```typescript
// BAD
console.log(`[LiftDropTrack] ${msg}`);
console.log(`[Animator] Loading…`);

// GOOD — failure (filterable)
error("tick", `Animation run "${name}" failed`, e, {
    animationId: id,
    triggerId: sourceTriggerId
});

// GOOD — lifecycle
log("animation", `Animation "${name}" started`, {
    kind: "animationStarted",
    animationId: id,
    triggerId: triggerId,
    trainIndex: context.trainIndex
});
```

- Temporary debug: still use `log`/`error` with a clear `area`; remove or keep only if Simon wants it permanent.
